<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIA BEAT MUNSTER 55-19.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIA BEAT MUNSTER 55-19.</headline>
<dateline>LIMERICK, Ireland 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia beat Munster 55-19 (halftime 24-9) in a tour match on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Australia - Tries: Ben Tune, Totai Kefu, David Campese (2), Alistair Murdoch (2), Sam Payne, Owen Finegan, Jason Little. Conversions: Steve Larkham (5)</p>
<p>Ireland - Try: Kilian Keane. Conversion: Keane Penalties: Keane (3). Dropped goal: Pat Murray.</p>
</text>
